# ============================================================
# EGFR - erlotinib binding site analysis
# Structure: PDB 1M17 (EGFR kinase domain with erlotinib)
#
# Purpose: locate the gatekeeper residue, measure its contacts
# with erlotinib, and produce a figure of the binding site.
#
# Run with:  open egfr_analysis.cxc
# Lines starting with # are comments and are not executed.
# ============================================================


# ---- 1. Start from a clean state -------------------------
# Closing everything first prevents duplicate models.
# A duplicate structure silently multiplies contact counts,
# which produces a wrong answer with no error message.

close all


# ---- 2. Load the structure -------------------------------
# 1M17 is fetched directly from the Protein Data Bank.
# It is the EGFR tyrosine kinase domain (residues 671-998 of
# EGFR_HUMAN) crystallised with erlotinib bound.

open 1M17


# ---- 3. Remove crystallographic water --------------------
# Water molecules from the crystal obscure the view and are
# not needed for this analysis.

hide solvent


# ---- 4. Locate the ligand --------------------------------
# Erlotinib has the PDB chemical component ID AQ4 and is
# stored as residue 999 of chain A in this file.
# info atoms lists its atom names - needed because the names
# are specific to each ligand and cannot be guessed.

info atoms /A:999


# ---- 5. Display the drug ---------------------------------
# Ball-and-stick in yellow so it is clearly distinguishable
# from the protein.

select ligand
view sel
style sel ball
color sel yellow


# ---- 6. Show the binding site ----------------------------
# Every residue with an atom within 5 A of the drug.
# These are the amino acids forming the ATP pocket.

show sel :<5 atoms
info residues sel


# ---- 7. IMPORTANT: residue numbering ---------------------
# This structure numbers residues from the MATURE protein,
# while the clinical literature numbers from the precursor
# including the 24-residue signal peptide.
#
#   offset = +24
#   clinical T790 (gatekeeper)     = THR 766 here
#   clinical C797 (osimertinib)    = CYS 773 here
#   clinical M793 (hinge)          = MET 769 here
#
# Verified by checking atom names: residue 790 in this file
# has CB/CG/CD1/CD2 (leucine), while residue 766 has
# OG1/CG2 (threonine). Getting this wrong would invalidate
# the whole analysis.


# ---- 8. Highlight the two key residues -------------------
# Red  = gatekeeper threonine, mutated to methionine in T790M
# Blue = cysteine that osimertinib binds covalently

~select
color /A:766 red
color /A:773 blue
show /A:766,773 atoms
style /A:766,773 stick


# ---- 9. Measure contacts ---------------------------------
# overlapCutoff -2 counts atom pairs whose van der Waals
# radii come within 2 A of touching, i.e. close but not
# necessarily overlapping.
# makePseudobonds draws them as green dashed lines.
#
# Expected result: 20 contacts between THR766 and erlotinib.
# If the number differs, check the Models panel for a
# duplicate structure before believing it.

contacts /A:766 restrict /A:999 overlapCutoff -2 makePseudobonds true


# ---- 10. Presentation settings ---------------------------
# White background reproduces better in documents than black.

set bgColor white
lighting soft


# ---- 11. Save the figure ---------------------------------
# supersample 3 renders at triple resolution then downsamples,
# which removes jagged edges.

save egfr_gatekeeper.png width 1600 supersample 3


# ---- 12. Save the session --------------------------------
# A .cxs file stores the full state, including the camera
# angle, so the exact view can be restored later.

save egfr_session.cxs


# ============================================================
# RESULT
# 20 contacts between THR766 (clinical T790) and erlotinib.
# The gatekeeper contacts the drug directly, so replacing it
# with the bulkier methionine encroaches on the space the
# inhibitor occupies - consistent with T790M conferring
# resistance to reversible quinazoline inhibitors.
# ============================================================
